# Surviving mutants that no test can tell apart from the code (equivalent mutants), or that change
# only a diagnostic, each with why (#326). One per line, as ci/mutants.sh prints them without their
# line and column numbers; text after `#` is the reason. A new survivor fails ci/mutants.sh until it
# is killed by a test or listed here.

# Raising a risk to the value it already has changes nothing.
crates/wicket-core/src/op.rs: replace > with >= in classify   # raising to an equal risk leaves it as it was
# 0.0.0.0, 255.255.255.255 and :: are also refused by `o[0] == 0`, `o[0] >= 240` and `s[..6] == [0; 6]`.
crates/wicket-core/src/op.rs: replace || with && in is_public_ip   # the broadcast and unspecified clauses are redundant
# The cost estimate (#183) is an upper bound checked when a token is made: these move its ties and
# exact boundary (a token costing exactly STEP_BUDGET, an empty pattern set), never a decision.
crates/wicket-authz/src/cost.rs: replace || with && in host_of   # a host predicate always has one term
crates/wicket-authz/src/cost.rs: replace > with >= in estimate   # a check with no patterns adds nothing; a tie changes the host named
crates/wicket-authz/src/cost.rs: replace > with >= in check   # a token costing exactly the budget: no fixture builds one
# Diagnostics only: nothing outside tests reads them.
crates/wicket-authz/src/decide.rs: replace Loaded::is_compiled -> bool with true   # every fixture token compiles
crates/wicket-authz/src/decide.rs: replace Loaded::last_fell_back -> bool with false   # no fixture falls back
